# Logging__LogLevel__Default=Debug
# Logging__LogLevel__Microsoft_EntityFrameworkCore=Information
# AllowedHosts=*

# STAGING PROFILE:
# ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Staging
# Logging__LogLevel__Default=Information
# AllowedHosts=staging.kromic.in

# PRODUCTION PROFILE:
# ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Production
# Logging__LogLevel__Default=Warning
# Logging__LogLevel__Microsoft_AspNetCore=Error
# AllowedHosts=kromic.in;api.kromic.in;store.kromic.in

# ============================================================================
# NOTES & GUIDELINES
# ============================================================================

# 1. ENVIRONMENT VARIABLE NAMING CONVENTION:
#    - Use double underscores (__) to denote section separators
#    - Example: "Jwt__Secret" maps to "Jwt" section, "Secret" property
#    - Example: "Database__ConnectionString" maps to "Database" section, "ConnectionString" property

# 2. REQUIRED vs OPTIONAL:
#    [REQUIRED FOR STARTUP]:
#    - ConnectionStrings__DefaultConnection
#    - Jwt__Secret (minimum 32 characters)
#    - Jwt__Issuer
#    - Jwt__Audience
#    - MultiTenancy__ReservedSubdomains
#    - MultiTenancy__ExcludedSubdomains
#    - Cors__AllowedOrigins
#
#    [OPTIONAL - HAVE DEFAULTS]:
#    - All JWT expiration settings
#    - All logging levels
#    - ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT
#    - AllowedHosts

# 3. VALIDATION:
#    - Application startup will FAIL if required configuration is missing or invalid
#    - JWT secrets must be >= 32 characters (enforced on startup)
#    - CORS origins must be valid URIs (enforced on startup)
#    - Multi-tenancy subdomains validated for format (enforced on startup)

# 4. SECURITY BEST PRACTICES:
#    - NEVER commit .env files with real secrets to version control
#    - NEVER share API keys or secrets
#    - Use strong random secrets (64+ characters) for Jwt__Secret in production
#    - Use HTTPS URLs for Cors__AllowedOrigins in production
#    - Rotate secrets periodically in production
#    - Use environment variable management systems (AWS Secrets Manager, Azure Key Vault, etc.) in production

# 5. RESERVED FOR FUTURE:
#    - All [RESERVED] configurations are placeholders for planned features
#    - These sections will be implemented in upcoming phases
#    - Reference documentation files in /docs folder for implementation details
#    - Uncomment and fill in when corresponding features are implemented

# 6. DEVELOPMENT VS PRODUCTION:
#    Development:
#    - Use localhost connection strings
#    - Use shorter token expirations (easier testing)
#    - Include localhost in CORS origins
#    - Enable detailed logging
#
#    Production:
#    - Use remote connection strings with strong passwords
#    - Use appropriate token expirations (15-30 mins for access tokens)
#    - Use HTTPS URLs in CORS
#    - Enable performance-appropriate logging (Warning or Error level)
#    - Ensure all API keys and secrets are strong

# 7. COMMON ISSUES & TROUBLESHOOTING:
#    - App fails to start with "ConnectionStrings:DefaultConnection must be configured"
#      → Solution: Ensure ConnectionStrings__DefaultConnection is set
#
#    - JWT token validation fails
#      → Solution: Verify Jwt__Secret, Jwt__Issuer, Jwt__Audience match frontend
#
#    - CORS requests blocked
#      → Solution: Add request origin to Cors__AllowedOrigins (must include scheme and port)
#
#    - Tenant resolution fails
#      → Solution: Verify subdomain not in MultiTenancy__ExcludedSubdomains

# ============================================================================
